ngredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">packet</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Knorr Savory Gravy Mix (chicken-style)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a rich flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">low-sodium chicken broth (or vegetable broth)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds depth and taste</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">unsalted butter</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">provides creaminess</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Optional Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">all-purpose flour</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for extra thickness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">onion powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">enhances the savory flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a burst of aroma</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Seasoning</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt and freshly ground black pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">to taste</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-3032-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3032\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Medium saucepan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking the gravy</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 whisk&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing ingredients</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-3032-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-3032-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3032\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3032-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Melt the Butter &#8211; In a medium saucepan, melt the butter over medium heat. Let it melt completely, creating a lovely base for your gravy.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3032-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Make the Roux &#8211; Whisk in the flour and cook for 1–2 minutes to form a light roux. This will give your gravy that nice, thick texture.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3032-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Add Chicken Broth &#8211; Gradually pour in the chicken broth, whisking constantly until smooth. This is where the magic starts to happen!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3032-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Mix in the Seasonings &#8211; Add the Knorr gravy mix, onion powder, and garlic powder; whisk until fully combined. Your kitchen will smell amazing!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3032-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Simmer and Thicken &#8211; Bring the mixture to a gentle simmer and cook for 3–5 minutes, stirring occasionally, until thickened. Keep an eye on it; you want it just right!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3032-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Season and Serve &#8211; Season with salt and pepper to taste, then remove from heat and serve immediately. Enjoy your delicious homemade Knorr gravy!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-3032-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>100</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>2g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>12g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients for your delicious Knorr gravy recipe!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Delicious-Knorr-Gravy-Recipe-with-Fresh-Ingredients.webp\" alt=\"Two cups of Knorr gravy with flour, spices, garlic, and noodles on a wooden board - Knorr Gravy Recipe\" class=\"wp-image-3041\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Delicious-Knorr-Gravy-Recipe-with-Fresh-Ingredients.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Delicious-Knorr-Gravy-Recipe-with-Fresh-Ingredients-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 packet Knorr Savory <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gravy </a>Mix (chicken-style)</strong> – for a rich flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cups low-sodium chicken broth (or vegetable broth)</strong> – adds depth and taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tbsp unsalted butter</strong> – provides creaminess</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tbsp all-purpose flour (optional)</strong> – for extra thickness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tsp onion powder</strong> – enhances the savory flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tsp garlic powder</strong> – adds a burst of aroma</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt and freshly ground black pepper</strong> – to taste</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-the-best-knorr-gravy-recipe\"><strong>How to Make the Best Knorr Gravy Recipe</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful Knorr gravy recipe is perfect for enhancing your meals. With a preparation time of just 5 minutes and a cooking time of 10 minutes, you’ll have a rich and flavorful gravy ready in no time!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Preparation-of-Knorr-Gravy-Recipe.webp\" alt=\"Visual guide for preparing Knorr Gravy Recipe, illustrating melting butter, creating roux, pouring in chicken broth, and mixing in seasonings.\" class=\"wp-image-3040\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Preparation-of-Knorr-Gravy-Recipe.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Preparation-of-Knorr-Gravy-Recipe-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Melt the Butter</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a medium saucepan, melt the butter over medium heat. Let it melt completely, creating a lovely base for your gravy.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Make the Roux</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Whisk in the flour and cook for 1–2 minutes to form a light roux. This will give your gravy that nice, thick texture.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Add Chicken Broth</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gradually pour in the chicken broth, whisking constantly until smooth. This is where the magic starts to happen!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Mix in the Seasonings</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the Knorr gravy mix, onion powder, and garlic powder; whisk until fully combined. Your kitchen will smell amazing!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Simmer and Thicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bring the mixture to a gentle simmer and cook for 3–5 minutes, stirring occasionally, until thickened. Keep an eye on it; you want it just right!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Season and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Season with salt and pepper to taste, then remove from heat and serve immediately. Enjoy your delicious homemade Knorr gravy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Sauce</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot over your favorite dishes!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-knorr-gravy-recipe\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making knorr gravy recipe</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Start with hot water for a smoother consistency.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Whisk continuously to avoid lumps and ensure even mixing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a pinch of garlic powder for extra flavor depth.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For a richer taste, use vegetable broth instead of water.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let it simmer for a few minutes to enhance the flavors.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-knorr-gravy-recipe\"><strong>How to Serve this knorr gravy recipe</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pour over mashed potatoes for a comforting classic.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a savory sauce for roasted vegetables.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle on grilled chicken or turkey for added flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with rice or quinoa for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with biscuits for a delicious brunch option.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a dipping sauce for breadsticks or pretzels.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can prepare and store your Knorr gravy recipe for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow gravy to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refrigerate for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the gravy completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use freezer-safe containers or bags.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Leave some space for expansion.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 3 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat on the stovetop over low heat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of broth or water for consistency.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir frequently until heated through.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. How do you use Knorr gravy mix?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Using Knorr gravy mix is simple! Just combine the mix with water according to the package instructions, usually in a saucepan. Stir it over medium heat until it thickens, and you’ll have a delicious gravy ready to serve over your favorite dishes like mashed potatoes or roasted vegetables.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What is the 3 2 1 rule for gravy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The 3 2 1 rule for gravy is a handy guideline: for every 3 cups of liquid, use 2 tablespoons of gravy mix, and it will yield about 1 cup of gravy. This rule helps you achieve the perfect consistency and flavor every time you make gravy, ensuring it’s neither too thick nor too thin.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What can I add to packet gravy to make it better?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To enhance packet gravy, consider adding sautéed onions, garlic, or mushrooms for depth of flavor. You can also mix in a splash of soy sauce or Worcestershire sauce for umami, or even a bit of cream for richness. Fresh herbs like thyme or parsley can brighten it up, making it taste homemade!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What is the ratio of gravy mix to water?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The typical ratio for Knorr gravy mix is about 1 tablespoon of mix to 1 cup of water. However, always check the specific instructions on the package, as different flavors may have slightly different ratios. Adjusting the amount of water can help you achieve your desired thickness for the gravy.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have the best Knorr gravy recipe in your hands, it’s time to whip it up and savor the deliciousness! Remember, it’s all about those simple ingredients coming together to create something truly special. So gather your loved ones, pour the gravy over your favorite dishes, and enjoy the warmth and joy it brings to your table!</p>\n",
